CCWTEST  TITLE 'CCWTEST - CAN A SOURCE MACRO SHADOW THE CCW INSTRUCTION'
         PRINT GEN,DATA
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*  ONE QUESTION, DECIDED BY EXPERIMENT RATHER THAN BY ARGUMENT.        *
*                                                                     *
*  CP HAS 240 CCW STATEMENTS IN 23 NUCLEUS MODULES.  `CCW` IS          *
*  ASSEMBLER XF'S OWN INSTRUCTION AND EMITS THE FORMAT-0 LAYOUT ONLY;  *
*  XF HAS NO CCW1, WHICH ARRIVED WITH ASSEMBLER H.  SO WHEN REAL       *
*  STORAGE OUTGROWS 16 MB AND FORMAT-1 CCWS BECOME NECESSARY (R-27),   *
*  THE COST IS EITHER                                                  *
*                                                                     *
*    ONE MACRO,  IF A SOURCE MACRO NAMED CCW TAKES PRECEDENCE OVER     *
*                THE ASSEMBLER INSTRUCTION OF THE SAME NAME, OR        *
*    240 EDITS,  IF IT DOES NOT.                                       *
*                                                                     *
*  I CLAIMED THE FORMER IN 17-CARRY-FORWARD-64.MD WITHOUT CHECKING.    *
*  THIS MODULE CHECKS.  IT DEFINES A CCW MACRO THAT EMITS A            *
*  RECOGNISABLE EIGHT BYTES, THEN USES CCW TWICE.  WITH PRINT GEN THE  *
*  LISTING SHOWS WHICH WON:                                            *
*                                                                     *
*    X'DDDDDDDDDDDDDDDD'  THE MACRO WON  -- ONE MACRO FIXES 240 SITES  *
*    X'0200100000000050'  THE INSTRUCTION WON -- 240 EDITS, OR OPSYN   *
*                                                                     *
*  A THIRD OUTCOME IS POSSIBLE AND WOULD ALSO BE AN ANSWER: THE        *
*  ASSEMBLER MAY REJECT THE DEFINITION OUTRIGHT.                       *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         MACRO
&NAME    CCW   &CODE,&ADDR,&FLAGS,&COUNT
&NAME    DC    8X'DD'         MACRO EXPANSION MARKER
         MEND
         SPACE 2
CCWTEST  CSECT
DATA     DS    CL80
         SPACE 1
*  TWO USES, WITH OPERANDS THE ASSEMBLER INSTRUCTION WOULD ACCEPT, SO
*  THAT WHICHEVER WINS PRODUCES EIGHT BYTES AND THE LISTING IS READABLE
*  EITHER WAY.
FIRST    CCW   X'02',DATA,X'00',80
SECOND   CCW   X'01',DATA,X'40',16
         SPACE 1
*  A CONTROL: DC IS DEFINITELY THE ASSEMBLER'S, AND NOTHING SHADOWS IT.
THIRD    DC    X'0000000000000000'
         SPACE 2
         END
